      "header": "(mi.)nlSpringDamperClipped",
      "summary": "Implementation of a non-linear viscoelastic spring-damper interaction containing a cubic term (function of distance^3), bound by an upper linear stiffness (hard-clipping). This bounding means that when faced with strong displacements, the interaction profile will \"clip\" at a given point and never produce forces higher than the bounding equivalent linear spring, stopping models from becoming unstable. So far the interaction clips \"hard\" (with no soft-knee spline interpolation, etc.)",
